ns were omitted, nor offer a `limit` knob to raise the cap from within the framing. I had to infer there were more hits than 20. The default `limit=20` is fine, but the truncation footer should ideally show the omitted count so I know whether to widen the search or move on.\n- **Lost context**: No. The error message and the successful second call together gave me everything I needed; I never lost track of which query or which mode I was running.\n- **Worked as expected**: `fs_search` errored cleanly with an enumerated list of valid values (very usable), and the `matches` mode did exactly what was wanted — regions with match lines, context, paths, and line ranges ready to paste into `fs_read_file` windows. The `path`/`start_line`/`end_line` provenance on each region is strong.\n- **Wasted turns**: One wasted turn on the `regions` typo, which is on the caller, not the tool. No wasted turns caused by tool behavior.", "tool_calls": []}, "event_id": "ev-000060", "harness_id": "fa-inner-loop@0.1.0", "kind": "model_msg", "parent_event_id": "", "run_id": "cae-s127-search-removed-mode-1788528805-1250437", "session_id": "session-6aec5b2dad6444abb109d1214f481072", "tool_call_id": "", "tool_name": "", "ts": "2026-09-04T13:38:17Z"}
